Issues & Mistakes

This is not valid plain HTML; {% block content %}{% endblock %} is a Django template syntax. In a pure frontend project, it will show up as-is in the browser.
document.write() inside js loadpage() breaks modern practice — it rewrites the whole DOM and affects SPA-style extensibility.
Some img and icon references in JS-injected content may miss alt and aria attributes (accessibility requirement).

JavaScript

Well modularized: each feature (form validation, smooth scroll, portfolio modal, blog filter, load-more, intersection animations) isolated into its own init function — excellent maintainability.
Uses clean DOMContentLoaded event handling.
Validation logic robust and UX-friendly (live feedback, success message).
IntersectionObserver correctly implemented for animations with thresholds.
The only major flaw is document.write() (should be replaced with DOM injection or template rendering).
Uses safe timeouts, proper async UI feedback, and no redundant global variables.
Good use of querySelectorAll, forEach, and template literals.

Improvements

Remove the Django template tags and replace with normal HTML content or placeholders suitable for frontend development.
Replace document.write() with HTML templates.
Validate accessibility via ARIA for decorative icons and alt attributes for all images.
Optimize JS size by moving static content data to a HTML for scalability.

